{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/26","id":4382655947,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABBToFyw","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/26","diff_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/26.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/26.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/26","number":26,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Cover every hdl/ module in the portability gate, and stop re-parsing the design once per top","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #25.\n\n`syn/yosys/run.sh` now covers every module under `hdl/`, enforces that it does,\nand reads the lowered design with `read_verilog -defer` in a bounded process\npool. **38 tops in 33.0 s, against 32 tops in 67.5 s.**\n\n## The coverage half, which is the load-bearing one\n\n`hdl/` declares 38 modules. The `tops` array named 32, and `hierarchy -top`\nover those 32 reached exactly those 32 — the other six were not covered\ntransitively either:\n\n`KL_acmp_nvm_shadow`, `KL_mrp_strip`, `KL_pp_dispatch_fifo`,\n`KL_srp_admission`, `KL_srp_top`, `protocol_processor_top`.\n\nThat gap is not theoretical. Injecting a fault into `KL_srp_top` — a module in\nno top — and running both forms of this script over it, with nothing else\nchanged:\n\n| fault injected into `KL_srp_top` | gate as it stands | this PR |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| instance of an undefined module | **rc=0 — missed** | rc=1 — `YOSYS FAIL KL_srp_top: ERROR: Module \\_absent_module … is not part of the design` |\n| syntax error | rc=1 — caught (by `sv2v`) | rc=1 — caught (by `sv2v`) |\n\nAn unresolved instance is exactly what `hierarchy -check` exists to catch, and\nit walked through. Note also which module is on that list:\n`protocol_processor_top` is the subject of #22, whose 44 use-before-declaration\nidentifiers were found by the integrator's Vivado front end rather than here —\nbecause this gate has never made it a top.\n\nAll six elaborate cleanly today, so this is a gap and not a latent defect.\n\n### The array is now enforced\n\nThe script derives the declared-module list from the sources and refuses if it\nand `tops` disagree, in either direction — a module with no top, or a top\nnaming a module that no longer exists. Its own header has said the array is\nauthoritative since it was written; nothing made that true. Proved by dropping\nan entry:\n\n```\n$ ./syn/yosys/run.sh          # with KL_srp_top removed from tops\nmodules declared under hdl/ with no entry in the tops array:\n  KL_srp_top\nextend tops (hdl/README rule 2) - the array is the authoritative list\n$ echo $?\n1\n```\n\n## The speed half\n\nThe script lowered the whole tree into one 21,912-line `all.v` and then started\none `yosys` per top, each beginning with `read_verilog all.v`. Measured here\n(`yosys 0.66`, `sv2v 0.0.13`; `sv2v` is 5.1 s on top of every variant):\n\n| variant | 32 tops | 38 tops |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| as it stood: one process per top, full `read_verilog` | 39.65 s | 52.60 s |\n| one process, parse once, `design -save` / `design -load` | 9.34 s | — |\n| one process per top, `read_verilog -defer` | 10.31 s | — |\n| bounded pool + `-defer` (this PR) | 1.25 s | **5.68 s** |\n\nEnd to end, including `sv2v` and the unchanged `synth_xilinx` BRAM regression:\n**67.46 s → 33.01 s**, with six more modules covered.\n\n`-defer` costs no coverage here, and that was controlled rather than assumed —\nit is the table at the top of this PR. A syntax error is caught either way, by\n`sv2v`, before Yosys reads anything; an unresolved instance in a module that is\nin no top is missed either way. `-defer` postpones elaboration, and what\nprovides elaboration coverage is the `tops` array, which this PR completes.\n\nFor the record in the other direction: `-defer` is **not** a general speed-up.\nOn the integrator's `syn/yosys/run.sh`, where each top is handed its own source\nlist, it removes 82–89% of the `read_verilog` step, that step is 0.5% of the\nrun, the gate does not get faster (−1.0% and +0.3% on the two heaviest tops)\nand it moves the cell count by +0.08% and +1.3%. It was measured and rejected\nthere — kebag-logic/milan-fpga#288. It belongs here because here, and only\nhere, one file holding every module is read once per top.\n\n## Reporting\n\nThe pool's own output interleaves, so it is discarded and the verdict is\nprinted **in inventory order** from per-top status files — a gate whose report\nreorders between runs cannot be diffed between runs. A top with no status file\nis reported as a failure, not skipped: a worker that died without recording a\nverdict is not a pass.\n\n`YOSYS_JOBS` overrides the pool width; it defaults to the online CPU count,\ncapped at 16.\n\n## Not changed\n\nThe `synth_xilinx` / `select -assert-count 6 t:RAMB36E1` regression gate is\nuntouched and still passes, the elaboration program per top is the same\n`hierarchy -check; proc; opt_clean`, and no RTL is modified.\n\n## Validation\n\n```\n$ ./syn/yosys/run.sh\nYOSYS OK  KL_aecp_ucpu\n… 38 lines …\nYOSYS XILINX OK  KL_aecp_engine\n$ echo $?\n0\n```\n\n38 `YOSYS OK`, 0 `YOSYS FAIL`, `YOSYS XILINX OK`, 33.01 s. Baseline on `main`\nat the same head: 32 `YOSYS OK`, `YOSYS XILINX OK`, 67.46 s.\n\nBoth degenerate cases above were run and are reproduced by injecting into\n`hdl/srp/KL_srp_top.sv` and by removing one name from `tops`.\n","created_at":"2026-08-28T07:27:44Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T17:00:50Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/26/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/26/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/26/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/statuses/7f35ed2abbf8565f1a117db2e10a1890feeddd52","head":{"label":"Mister-M-alt:25-cover-every-module-and-stop-reparsing","ref":"25-cover-every-module-and-stop-reparsing","sha":"7f35ed2abbf8565f1a117db2e10a1890feeddd52","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_